## Part B. The hand-off folder, the PM report, and the plan evidence

The maker builds the hand-off folder with one node script,
`measure/runs/asset_storytime_l2u2_look1_20261111/make-handoff-look1.mjs`. The script makes hard
links of the 4 delivered PNG files, copies manifest.json and the spend log, writes the contact
sheet with sharp, writes README.md, and writes MANIFEST.txt last.

### The defaults of this step

The brief leaves some choices open. The maker takes these defaults and records them here.

1. The contact sheet uses the form of handoff-retry1.mjs: a cell of 300 px, a pad of 16 px, a gap of
   12 px, a label band of 30 px, and the row id under the pair, centered.
2. The row order of the contact sheet is hat-pip first and the T-shirt second, as the brief names.
3. The MANIFEST.txt comment block holds the title of the folder, a line on the 2 delivery jobs, a
   line on the owner acceptance of the hat-pip row, and the check command. It names no acceptance of
   the T-shirt picture.
4. The README.md and the pm-report.md quote the PM order and the owner words word for word. They
   keep the other sentences in the voice of the maker.
5. The builder refuses to run when the hand-off folder exists. It never writes into the 6 old
   folders, the cover folder, or the delivery folder.

### The build

The maker wrote the script and ran it once with node. The run gave exit status 0. It linked the 4
delivered PNG files, copied manifest.json and spend-log.tsv, wrote contact-sheet.png at 644 x 724
with 2 pairs, wrote README.md, and wrote MANIFEST.txt last.

